$WW,1$$FG,5$$TX+CX,"Requirements for ZealOS"$$FG$

$FG,5$User Skills Required$FG$
* Knowledge of the $FG,2$C$FG$ programming language.

$FG,5$Supported Hardware$FG$
* $FG,4$$TX,"x86_64",HTML="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amd64#AMD64"$$FG$ PC compatible computer.  (Obviously, you need 64-bit hardware for a 64-bit operating system.)

* 32-bit color $FG,2$high-res VBE$FG$ graphics.

* Most$FG$ keyboards and mice.

* Minimum $TX,"256Meg",D="DD_MEM_MIN_MEG"$ RAM.

* Internal PC Speakers.

* CD/DVD-ROMs (not SCSI), RedSea or ISO9660 file system.

* SATA hard drives. (SATA, mSATA, m.2)

* USB mass-storage flash drives using xHCI, Bulk-Only Transport, SCSI transparent commands, LUN 0, and 512-byte sectors.

* A few networking cards.

$FG,5$Unsupported Hardware$FG$
* No graphics acceleration.

* No sound cards.

* No USB Attached SCSI (UAS), multi-LUN USB storage, or USB storage with non-512-byte sectors. Mac mini live boot primarily uses the firmware-loaded UEFI image and installs to internal AHCI SATA ($LK,"InstallMacMini.DD",A="FI:::/Doc/InstallMacMini.DD"$).

* Native $FG,2$USB keyboard/mouse$FG$ via xHCI when available; minimal UHCI HID for UTM/QEMU PC UI input; $FG,2$PS/2$FG$ fallback otherwise.

* No printers.
